+You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License along with
+GCC; see the file COPYING3.  If not see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
+
+This header carries what the target mandates rather than what a caller
+remembers.  Everything in it is a value some package can forget to pass, which
+is the definition of a thing that belongs here instead of in a makefile.  The
+target definition it answers to is doc/target-definition.md.  */
+
+/* The red zone is honoured on this platform.  The psABI reserves 128 bytes
+   below %rsp and a conforming platform leaves them alone; this one does, at
+   the delivery site, the way a Linux kernel does.  DR-0006 chose that
+   direction and WP-43 built and certified the repair: Cygwin's signal
+   delivery reserves the 128 bytes before it builds a handler frame, and the
+   reservation's cost measured negligible.
+
+   So the -mno-red-zone scaffolding this block once carried, which made every
+   leaf adjust %rsp and announced in its prologue that this was not quite the
+   ABI it claimed, is retired: the subtarget default below no longer disables
+   the red zone, so a leaf uses it as System V code does, kept whole by the
+   delivery repair for compiled and hand-written code alike.  The record
+   retiring the flag supersedes DR-0006, and WP-16's ledger of the hand-written
+   assembly the flag never reached closes with it.  -mred-zone and
+   -mno-red-zone stay selectable as on any x86-64 target; neither is forced.
+   Added to i386/unix.h's set rather than replacing it, which is the whole of
+   the difficulty.  That header defines the default as MASK_80387, MASK_IEEE_FP
+   and MASK_FLOAT_RETURNS, and a target header that assigns instead of ORing
+   silently turns the x87 off.  Nothing complains at configure time; libgcc
+   fails much later building __mulxc3 with "x87 register return with x87
+   disabled", which reads like a libgcc bug and is not one.  */
+#undef  TARGET_SUBTARGET_DEFAULT
+#define TARGET_SUBTARGET_DEFAULT \
+	(MASK_80387 | MASK_IEEE_FP | MASK_FLOAT_RETURNS)
+
+/* config.guess cannot read the vendor field off uname here: sysname is Linux
+   by design, so that the thousands of configure scripts branching on it keep
+   working.  It asks the compiler instead, the way it already asks which libc
+   it is looking at, and this is the answer it asks for.  Removing this define
+   makes a native build silently configure as x86_64-pc-linux-gnu.  */
+#undef  TARGET_OS_CPP_BUILTINS
+#define TARGET_OS_CPP_BUILTINS()		\
+  do						\
+    {						\
+      GNU_USER_TARGET_OS_CPP_BUILTINS ();	\
+      ANDROID_TARGET_OS_CPP_BUILTINS ();	\
+      builtin_define ("__ELFSYSVNT__");		\
+    }						\
+  while (0)
